.TH ZAP 1 "October 2026" "zap 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zap \- native Zig AUR helper using libalpm and systemd run0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zap
.I command
.RI [ packages ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
zap searches repository and AUR packages, resolves dependencies, reviews
PKGBUILDs, builds packages as the invoking user, and runs native libalpm
transactions through systemd run0 and polkit. It never builds as root.
System changes require an installed root-owned /usr/bin/zap and a terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search TERM (-Ss)
Search cached repositories and live AUR metadata.
.TP
.B info PACKAGES (-Si)
Display package details, dependencies and update dates.
.TP
.B install PACKAGES (-S)
Review, build and install packages and their dependencies.
.TP
.B build PACKAGES
Review and build AUR packages without installing. Build dependencies must
already be installed.
.TP
.B get PACKAGES
Fetch AUR sources into the user cache without executing them.
.TP
.B upgrade (-Syu)
Refresh and upgrade repositories, then upgrade installed AUR packages.
.TP
.B updates (-Qu)
Check cached repositories and live AUR for newer versions.
.TP
.B list [PACKAGES] (-Q)
List installed versions, installation dates and reasons.
.TP
.B foreign (-Qm)
List installed packages absent from repositories.
.TP
.B remove PACKAGES (-R)
Remove packages with native dependency checks.
.TP
.B orphans
List dependency packages without required or optional users.
.TP
.B autoremove
Review and remove orphan dependencies.
.TP
.B clean [BASES] (-Sc)
Confirm and clear all or selected package-base directories in the user's AUR source/build cache.
.TP
.B version (--version)
Display the version and libalpm ABI.
.TP
.B select TERM
Search and choose numbered packages or ranges for reviewed installation.
.TP
.B local-search TERM (-Qs), localinfo PACKAGES (-Qi)
Search installed packages or display installed metadata and reverse dependencies.
.TP
.B build-local DIRS (-B), install-local DIRS (-Bi)
Copy local PKGBUILDs and static .SRCINFO into fresh cache snapshots, resolve
and review dependencies, then build or build and install. Copy every regular
source file except Git metadata, top-level src/pkg trees and package archives.
Reject symlinks and special files. Preserve the original checkout.
.TP
.B install-files FILES (-U)
Inspect and hash local archives. The worker snapshots them and enforces local
signature policy before installation. No code executes during inspection.
.TP
.B pkgbuild PACKAGES (-Gp), get PACKAGES (-G)
Print PKGBUILDs or fetch AUR sources without executing them.
.TP
.B files PACKAGES (-Ql), owns FILES (-Qo)
List installed file paths or find their installed owners.
.TP
.B check [PACKAGES] (-Qk)
Check installed file presence. Return failure if files are missing.
This is not content/checksum verification.
.TP
.B reason PACKAGES --asdeps|--asexplicit (-D)
Confirm and change installation reasons under the ALPM lock.
.TP
.B stats (-Ps), news (-Pw)
Show installed counts, sizes and largest packages, or recent Arch news links.
Read intervention instructions before upgrading.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Skip builds, escalation and system changes. Install/build plans can fetch
sources and ask for a provider. Final repository changes are resolved by
libalpm during the actual transaction. get and pkgbuild fetch sources and reject this option.
.TP
.B --devel
Include installed -git, -svn, -hg and -bzr packages for rebuild during updates
or upgrade. Also includes -cvs, -darcs and -fossil. This requests rebuilds
rather than tracking upstream commits.
.TP
.B --recursive
Also remove unneeded dependencies with remove.
.TP
.B --nosave
Discard backup configuration during remove. -Rns combines --recursive and
--nosave.
.TP
.B --aur, --repo
Limit search, select, info, install, updates and upgrade to the requested
source. Dependencies can come from either source. -Sua and -Qua select
AUR-only upgrade and updates. AUR-only upgrades do not refresh repositories;
repository upgrades always perform a full repository upgrade.
.TP
.B --needed
Skip current or newer installed targets during install, while applying
requested reason changes. Without this flag, reinstall requested packages
including same-version AUR rebuilds.
.TP
.B --asdeps, --asexplicit
Override installation reasons for requested packages, not their dependencies.
Also required with reason. Contradictory flags fail.
.TP
.B --sandbox, --no-sandbox
Isolate all makepkg phases by default using bubblewrap. System and package
database mounts are read-only. Only the checkout is writable on the host,
with Git metadata read-only. Give each phase an empty environment and private
home without credentials, agents or desktop sockets. Network access remains
available for downloads. Probe before installation; failure never falls back.
User makepkg configuration and signing keys are unavailable in the sandbox.
--no-sandbox explicitly runs approved code with the invoking user's permissions.
.TP
.B --rebuildtree
Rebuild installed foreign dependencies during builds, installs and upgrades.
Reject combination with --needed; dependency cycles fail explicitly.
.TP
.B --cleanafter
Remove untracked and ignored files after successful installation, retaining
tracked review sources. Only valid for commands that can install builds.
.TP
.B --quiet, -q
Print names only for search, local-search, updates, list, foreign, orphans,
and owns. files prints paths only. -Qq, -Qmq and -Qdtq are aliases.
.TP
.B --searchby FIELD
AUR search field: name, name-desc, maintainer, provides, depends,
makedepends, checkdepends or optdepends. Repository search remains unchanged.
.TP
.B --sortby FIELD
AUR search order: votes (default), popularity, name or modified.
.TP
.B --
End option parsing; remaining arguments are targets, including filenames.
.SH DATES
All dates are UTC. AUR results show last modification. Repository results
show build dates. Local listings show installation dates.
.SH SECURITY
PKGBUILDs execute arbitrary code after review. Default sandboxing limits host
access; --no-sandbox grants code the invoking user's permissions. The sandbox
uses the host toolchain and is not a clean chroot or network isolation. Every system transaction requires a separate final
confirmation and uses configured signature policies, ALPM locks and hooks.
Approved archives are copied into private root-owned staging and checked
against their SHA-256 digests before installation. AUR upgrades span several
transactions; earlier successful installs remain if a later build fails.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/pacman.conf
Repository configuration and package/signature policies.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/zap, $HOME/.cache/zap
User-owned AUR source and build cache.
.TP
.B /usr/bin/zap
Root-owned executable used by the transaction worker.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal styling.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Absolute user cache directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 130 on a cancelled operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR run0 (1),
.BR libalpm (3)
